<LegalLayout
  title="Website Privacy Policy and Data Practices | Local Service Rocket"
  description="How Local Service Rocket collects, uses, and protects personal information when you use our website or book onboarding. Read our privacy practices."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updated="September 9, 2026"
>
  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Local Service Rocket (“we,” “us,” or “our”) provides marketing, recruiting, and related services
    for residential home service businesses. We operate from Wellington, New Zealand, and serve
    clients primarily in the United States, Australia, and New Zealand.
  </p>
  <p>
    Contact: <a href="mailto:hello@localservicerocket.com">hello@localservicerocket.com</a> ·
    <a href="tel:8883716365">(888) 371-6365</a>
  </p>

  <h2>2. Scope</h2>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, share, and protect personal information when
    you visit <strong>localservicerocket.com</strong>, book a call, contact us, or otherwise engage
    with our marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Information we collect</h2>
  <p>We may collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Contact and business details</strong> you provide (name, email, phone, company name,
      trade, location, website, and related business information) when you book onboarding, email
      us, call us, or fill out forms.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Communications</strong> you send us, including notes from calls and emails.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Usage and device data</strong> such as IP address, browser type, pages viewed, referring
      URLs, and approximate location, collected through cookies, pixels, and similar technologies.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Advertising and analytics data</strong> from tools we use to measure site performance
      and ad campaigns (for example Google Analytics, Google Ads, and related tags).
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. How we use information</h2>
  <p>We use personal information to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Respond to inquiries and schedule onboarding or service calls</li>
    <li>Provide, manage, and improve our services</li>
    <li>Send service-related communications and, where permitted, marketing updates</li>
    <li>Measure website performance, improve content, and run advertising</li>
    <li>Comply with legal obligations and protect our rights and users</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Cookies and tracking</h2>
  <p>
    Our site may use cookies, pixels, and similar technologies for essential site function,
    analytics, and advertising. You can control cookies through your browser settings. Disabling
    some cookies may affect site features.
  </p>
  <p>
    Embedded third-party content (such as YouTube videos) may set their own cookies when you interact
    with that content. We load some embeds only after you choose to play them to reduce unnecessary
    tracking.
  </p>

  <h2>6. How we share information</h2>
  <p>We may share personal information with:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Service providers</strong> who help us operate the business (for example hosting,
      scheduling/booking tools such as LeadConnector, email, analytics, and advertising platforms).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Professional advisors</strong> when reasonably necessary (legal, accounting).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Authorities</strong> when required by law or to protect rights, safety, or security.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your personal information for money.</p>

  <h2>7. International transfers</h2>
  <p>
    We are based in New Zealand and work with clients and vendors in other countries, including the
    United States and Australia. Your information may be processed outside your home country. Where
    required, we take steps intended to protect that information appropriately.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Retention</h2>
  <p>
    We keep personal information only as long as needed for the purposes described above, including
    to provide services, meet legal or accounting requirements, resolve disputes, and enforce
    agreements - then we delete or anonymize it when retention is no longer necessary.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Security</h2>
  <p>
    We use reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational measures to protect personal
    information. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee
    absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, or restrict use of
    your personal information, or to object to certain processing (including marketing). To exercise
    these rights, email
    <a href="mailto:hello@localservicerocket.com">hello@localservicerocket.com</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    You may unsubscribe from marketing emails using the link in those messages, or by contacting us.
    Service and transactional messages may still be sent when needed.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Children’s privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Our services are directed to business owners and operators, not children. We do not knowingly
    collect personal information from anyone under 16. If you believe we have, contact us and we will
    take appropriate steps to delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Third-party links</h2>
  <p>
    Our site may link to third-party websites or tools. We are not responsible for their privacy
    practices. Review their policies before providing information.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date at the top will
    change when we do. Continued use of the site after updates means you accept the revised policy.
  </p>

  <h2>14. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this Privacy Policy or our data practices:<br />
    Local Service Rocket<br />
    Wellington, New Zealand<br />
    <a href="mailto:hello@localservicerocket.com">hello@localservicerocket.com</a><br />
    <a href="tel:8883716365">(888) 371-6365</a>
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
